cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EER in your research, please cite the following work."
title: "Epistemic Ecology Runtime: A Variational Framework for Continuous Belief Relaxation on Dynamic Epistemic Graphs"
abstract: >-
  We present the Epistemic Ecology Runtime (EER), a variational framework
  for aggregating continuous beliefs across dynamic epistemic graphs. All
  heuristic parameters are derived from a canonical Gaussian graphical
  model via empirical Bayes. We prove linear convergence without diagonal
  dominance (Ostrowski-Reich), establish formal anti-starvation guarantees
  for the priority scheduler, extend the framework to continuous-time
  projected differential inclusions, and provide an observational-data
  calibration pipeline.
